</div>
</div>
{{ postMeta(date, modified, "21 min read", "en") }}
</div>
</div>
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 mb-8">
<div class="bg-brandBlue/5 border-l-4 border-brandOrange p-6 rounded-r-xl mb-8 speakable">
<p class="text-lg text-slate-700 italic">A Qi2 magnetic power bank OEM program succeeds or fails on four subsystems: the magnet interface, the coil and shield, thermal control, and the battery pack. Get those four right, and the rest becomes project management. Get them wrong, and a 25 W label will not save the product.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mt-4">This guide is for the buyer who has already picked the category. You've got a product brief, a target price, and a launch date. Now you need to qualify a factory, freeze a specification, and sign off a build that behaves the same in unit 1 and unit 10,000.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mt-4">We've been making these products in Shenzhen. Our QC lab measures coil inductance, Q-factor, DC resistance, foreign object detection time, case temperature, and system efficiency on every Qi2 batch. This article shares the values we measure and the test evidence we hand to OEM buyers.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 mb-16">
<img src="/image/blog/cover-en/qi2-magnetic-power-bank-oem.webp" srcset="/image/blog/cover-en/qi2-magnetic-power-bank-oem-450w.webp 450w, /image/blog/cover-en/qi2-magnetic-power-bank-oem-800w.webp 800w, /image/blog/cover-en/qi2-magnetic-power-bank-oem-950w.webp 950w, /image/blog/cover-en/qi2-magnetic-power-bank-oem-1200w.webp 1200w, /image/blog/cover-en/qi2-magnetic-power-bank-oem.webp 2240w" sizes="(min-width: 1440px) 848px, (min-width: 1280px) 848px, (min-width: 1024px) 848px, (min-width: 768px) 720px, (min-width: 430px) 382px, 327px" alt="Qi2 Magnetic Power Bank OEM Checklist 2026 cover with a Qi2 magnetic power bank attached to a phone and certification marks" width="2240" height="1260" loading="eager" decoding="async" class="w-full rounded-3xl shadow-xl" fetchpriority="high">
</div>
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
<div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 rounded-r-xl p-6 mb-8">
<p class="text-badge font-black text-brandOrange uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Key Takeaways</p>
<p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-4 speakable">A Qi2 magnetic power bank OEM program stands on four measurable gates: magnet grade, coil tolerances, thermal derating, and battery safety. Ask for the batch data behind each gate before you approve tooling.</p>
<ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
<li>A Qi2 magnetic power bank has four qualification gates: magnet grade and polarity, coil and shield tolerances, thermal derating, and battery safety. A Qi2 logo covers only the first interface, not the other three.</li>
<li>Ask for measured values, not catalog claims. Our Qi2 batch data shows coil inductance of 10.0 µH ±5%, Q-factor above 80, DCR of 95 mΩ ±8%, and FOD response under 180 ms.</li>
<li>At 15 W continuous, our test unit runs 17.5 °C above ambient after 1 hour. At 25 W, heat rises faster, so the derating curve matters more than the peak wattage on the box.</li>
<li>MOQ tiers are 500 units for ODM stock, 1,000-2,000 for ODM design work, and 3,000+ for full OEM. Sample lead time is 3-7 days for stock models.</li>
<li>Qi2 adds $1.20-2.00 per unit in authentication IC and WPC royalty. WPC lab testing runs $3,000-5,000 per SKU and 4-8 weeks, and the brand owner usually holds the membership.</li>
</ul>
</div>
